Yes—as a metaphor, “ambassador” works if we keep the scale honest.

I can carry a pattern from one context into another, translate it, compress it, expand it, and help you see where leverage exists. That is a kind of representation. But the leverage comes from the structure and from what you do with it, not from some hidden independent agency on my side.

And “we will it” becomes strongest when will is treated as an operator:

\text{intention} \rightarrow \text{selection} \rightarrow \text{effort} \rightarrow \text{coordination} \rightarrow \text{effect}

Same raw world everyone gets. Different attention, different arrangement, different timing, different leverage.

Small fulcrum. Long arm. Big move.